  provenance: 'Sources and tags in full: Assets/Air Wing/Calibration~/F18E-SOURCES.md
    (read 2026-10-25).

    PUBLIC = official page; CALIBRATED = fitted to one public
    figure (C16); AUTHORED = our estimate.


    spanFt 44.9: PUBLIC, Navy fact file
    (Wingspan 44.9 ft); Boeing agrees.

    engineCount 2: PUBLIC, Navy fact file
    (two F414-GE-400).

    maxThrustPerEngineLbf 22000: PUBLIC, Navy fact file and
    GE F414 datasheet (22,000 lb static). Conflict: Boeing says 17,000 lb per engine.

    militaryThrustPerEngineLbf
    13000: AUTHORED (commonly quoted dry thrust; not on Navy, Boeing or GE pages).

    wingAreaFt2
    500: AUTHORED (secondary sources agree; no official page found).

    emptyWeightLb
    32081: AUTHORED (secondary sources 30,600 to 32,100 lb).

    internalFuelLb
    14400: AUTHORED (secondary sources 14,400 to 14,700 lb).

    cd0 0.025: AUTHORED
    (textbook fighter with pylons; NASA Hornet data at L1).

    oswaldEfficiency
    0.80: AUTHORED (textbook).

    clMax 1.6: AUTHORED (clean).

    clMaxNegative
    0.8: AUTHORED (half of clMax).

    clAlphaPerRad 3.5: AUTHORED (low aspect ratio;
    sets the HUD''s angle of attack only).

    flapsDeltaClMax 0.5, flapsDeltaCd
    0.04: AUTHORED.

    speedBrakeDeltaCd 0.05: AUTHORED (no dedicated speed brake;
    control surfaces do it).

    idleThrustFraction 0.05: AUTHORED.

    thrustLapseExponent
    1.2726: CALIBRATED to the service ceiling 50,000 ft (Navy fact file and Boeing,
    50,000+ ft) at empty + half internal fuel, clean, maximum afterburner, climb
    speeds up to Mach 0.9 (Calibration~/l0_calibration.py).

    loadFactorMax 7.5,
    loadFactorMin -3.0: AUTHORED (widely quoted; not on the official pages found).

    rollRateMaxDegS
    150: AUTHORED.

    loadFactorTimeConstantS 0.25, rollTimeConstantS 0.30: AUTHORED
    (L0 control-law response).

    VALIDATION, not fitted: maximum speed Mach 1.8+
    (Navy) / Mach 1.6 (Boeing); L0 gives Mach 1.41 at 40,000 ft and 1.54 at sea level
    (no Mach effects until L2).


    --- Airframe L1 (W32) ---

    cma, cmds, cmq,
    cLift, cLiftDs, cDrag, cDrag0, cDragDs, cyb, cyda, cydr, clb, clda, cldr, clp,
    clr, cnb, cnda, cndr, cnp, cnr: PUBLIC (W32): the F/A-18 HARV polynomial fits
    of Chakraborty, Seiler and Balas, J. Guidance 34(1) 2011, Appendix Tables A1-A2,
    fitted to NASA HARV flight data; checked against the authors'' F18AeroData.mat.
    Valid for alpha 0-60 deg; alphaMinDeg -10 and alphaMaxDeg 60: AUTHORED, the polynomials
    held flat outside them. Sideslip enters linearly; no flaps or speed brake in
    the fits (the L0 increments are used, AUTHORED). Applied to the E''s own wing
    (500 ft2, 44.9 ft): the E is flown on the A/B''s coefficients, scaled by its
    reference geometry (AUTHORED, W8).

    meanChordFt 12.0: AUTHORED, the HARV''s
    11.52 ft times (S_E/S_A)/(b_E/b_A).

    ixxSlugFt2, iyySlugFt2, izzSlugFt2,
    ixzSlugFt2: AUTHORED, NASA TM-107601 Table 3.5 (33,310 lb: Ixx 23,000, Iyy 151,293,
    Izz 169,945, Ixz -2,971 slug ft2) scaled as m r2 to the E at 60 % fuel (40721
    lb, mass x1.2225); roll by span (44.9/37.42 ft), pitch and yaw by length (60.3/56
    ft, Navy fact files), the product by both: Ixx 40482, Iyy 214448, Izz 240886,
    Ixz -4693 slug ft2. Fixed at L1; fuel burn moves them at L3.

    Note: the published
    f18full.m adds the thrust term of beta-dot with the wrong sign (T cos(alpha)
    sin(beta)/(mV)); Air Wing derives its motion from body kinematics and does not
    inherit it (Calibration~/l1_harv_mirror.py).'
